melody:
# Chorus (dotted rhythms of the 1908 edition written as straight eighths; the swing band swings them)
Oh, shine on, shine on, har-vest moon up in the sky;
B4 C5(2) B4(2) C5 B4 G#4 E4 C#4(2) ~C#4/ B#3/ C#4/ B4/ A4(2) ~A4 r
I ain't had no lov-in' since A-pril, Jan-u-a-ry, June or Ju-ly.
B4(2) ~B4 A4 B4 A4/ D5/ ~D5/ B4/ A4 G4/ E4/ ~D4/ r/ G4/ E4/ D4/ E4/ G4/ E4/ D4/ G4/ ~G4 r
Snow time ain't no time to stay out-doors and spoon; so
C5(2) B4(2) C5 B4 G#4 E4 C#4(2) ~C#4/ B#3/ C#4/ B4/ A4(2) ~A4 A4
shine on, shine on, har-vest moon, for me and my gal.
B4(2) A4(2) B4. A4/ D5 B4 G4. D4/ E4/ D4/ E4 G4(2) ~G4

